  25:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****           ##### COMP Peripheral features #####
  26:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****   ==============================================================================
  27:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c **** 
  28:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****   [..]
  29:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****       The STM32G4xx device family integrates seven analog comparators instances:
ARM GAS  C:\Users\ACER\AppData\Local\Temp\ccMsoCuI.s 			page 2


  30:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****       COMP1, COMP2, COMP3, COMP4, COMP5, COMP6 and COMP7.
  31:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****       (#) Comparators input minus (inverting input) and input plus (non inverting input)
  32:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****           can be set to internal references or to GPIO pins
  33:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****           (refer to GPIO list in reference manual).
  34:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c **** 
  35:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****       (#) Comparators output level is available using HAL_COMP_GetOutputLevel()
  36:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****           and can be redirected to other peripherals: GPIO pins (in mode
  37:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****           alternate functions for comparator), timers.
  38:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****           (refer to GPIO list in reference manual).
  39:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c **** 
  40:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****       (#) The comparators have interrupt capability through the EXTI controller
  41:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****           with wake-up from sleep and stop modes.
  42:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c **** 
  43:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****           From the corresponding IRQ handler, the right interrupt source can be retrieved
  44:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****           using macro __HAL_COMP_COMPx_EXTI_GET_FLAG().
  45:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c **** 
  46:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****             ##### How to use this driver #####
  47:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****   ==============================================================================
  48:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****   [..]
  49:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****       This driver provides functions to configure and program the comparator instances
  50:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****       of STM32G4xx devices.
  51:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c **** 
  52:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****       To use the comparator, perform the following steps:
  53:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c **** 
  54:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****       (#)  Initialize the COMP low level resources by implementing the HAL_COMP_MspInit():
  55:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****       (++) Configure the GPIO connected to comparator inputs plus and minus in analog mode
  56:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****            using HAL_GPIO_Init().
  57:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****       (++) If needed, configure the GPIO connected to comparator output in alternate function mode
  58:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****            using HAL_GPIO_Init().
  59:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****       (++) If required enable the COMP interrupt by configuring and enabling EXTI line in Interrupt
  60:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****            selecting the desired sensitivity level using HAL_GPIO_Init() function. After that enabl
  61:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****            interrupt vector using HAL_NVIC_EnableIRQ() function.
  62:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c **** 
  63:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****       (#) Configure the comparator using HAL_COMP_Init() function:
  64:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****       (++) Select the input minus (inverting input)
  65:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****       (++) Select the input plus (non-inverting input)
  66:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****       (++) Select the hysteresis
  67:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****       (++) Select the blanking source
  68:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****       (++) Select the output polarity
  69:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c **** 
  70:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****       -@@- HAL_COMP_Init() calls internally __HAL_RCC_SYSCFG_CLK_ENABLE()
  71:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****           to enable internal control clock of the comparators.
  72:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****           However, this is a legacy strategy. In future STM32 families,
  73:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****           COMP clock enable must be implemented by user in "HAL_COMP_MspInit()".
  74:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****           Therefore, for compatibility anticipation, it is recommended to
  75:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****           implement __HAL_RCC_SYSCFG_CLK_ENABLE() in "HAL_COMP_MspInit()".
  76:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c **** 
  77:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****       (#) Reconfiguration on-the-fly of comparator can be done by calling again
  78:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****           function HAL_COMP_Init() with new input structure parameters values.
  79:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c **** 
  80:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****       (#) Enable the comparator using HAL_COMP_Start() function.
  81:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c **** 
  82:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****       (#) Use HAL_COMP_TriggerCallback() or HAL_COMP_GetOutputLevel() functions
  83:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****           to manage comparator outputs (events and output level).
  84:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c **** 
  85:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****       (#) Disable the comparator using HAL_COMP_Stop() function.
  86:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c **** 
ARM GAS  C:\Users\ACER\AppData\Local\Temp\ccMsoCuI.s 			page 3


  87:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****       (#) De-initialize the comparator using HAL_COMP_DeInit() function.
  88:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c **** 
  89:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****       (#) For safety purpose, comparator configuration can be locked using HAL_COMP_Lock() function
  90:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****           The only way to unlock the comparator is a device hardware reset.
  91:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c **** 
  92:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****     *** Callback registration ***
  93:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****     =============================================
  94:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****     [..]
  95:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c **** 
  96:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****      The compilation flag USE_HAL_COMP_REGISTER_CALLBACKS, when set to 1,
  97:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****      allows the user to configure dynamically the driver callbacks.
  98:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****      Use Functions HAL_COMP_RegisterCallback()
  99:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****      to register an interrupt callback.
 100:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****     [..]
 101:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c **** 
 102:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****      Function HAL_COMP_RegisterCallback() allows to register following callbacks:
 103:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****        (+) TriggerCallback       : callback for COMP trigger.
 104:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****        (+) MspInitCallback       : callback for Msp Init.
 105:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****        (+) MspDeInitCallback     : callback for Msp DeInit.
 106:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****      This function takes as parameters the HAL peripheral handle, the Callback ID
 107:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****      and a pointer to the user callback function.
 108:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****     [..]
 109:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c **** 
 110:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****      Use function HAL_COMP_UnRegisterCallback to reset a callback to the default
 111:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****      weak function.
 112:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****     [..]
 113:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c **** 
 114:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****      HAL_COMP_UnRegisterCallback takes as parameters the HAL peripheral handle,
 115:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****      and the Callback ID.
 116:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****      This function allows to reset following callbacks:
 117:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****        (+) TriggerCallback       : callback for COMP trigger.
 118:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****        (+) MspInitCallback       : callback for Msp Init.
 119:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****        (+) MspDeInitCallback     : callback for Msp DeInit.
 120:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****      [..]
 121:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c **** 
 122:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****      By default, after the HAL_COMP_Init() and when the state is HAL_COMP_STATE_RESET
 123:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****      all callbacks are set to the corresponding weak functions:
 124:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****      example HAL_COMP_TriggerCallback().
 125:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****      Exception done for MspInit and MspDeInit functions that are
 126:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****      reset to the legacy weak functions in the HAL_COMP_Init()/ HAL_COMP_DeInit() only when
 127:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****      these callbacks are null (not registered beforehand).
 128:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****     [..]
 129:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c **** 
 130:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****      If MspInit or MspDeInit are not null, the HAL_COMP_Init()/ HAL_COMP_DeInit()
 131:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****      keep and use the user MspInit/MspDeInit callbacks (registered beforehand) whatever the state.
 132:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****      [..]
 133:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c **** 
 134:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****      Callbacks can be registered/unregistered in HAL_COMP_STATE_READY state only.
 135:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****      Exception done MspInit/MspDeInit functions that can be registered/unregistered
 136:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****      in HAL_COMP_STATE_READY or HAL_COMP_STATE_RESET state,
 137:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****      thus registered (user) MspInit/DeInit callbacks can be used during the Init/DeInit.
 138:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****     [..]
 139:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c **** 
 140:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****      Then, the user first registers the MspInit/MspDeInit user callbacks
 141:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****      using HAL_COMP_RegisterCallback() before calling HAL_COMP_DeInit()
 142:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****      or HAL_COMP_Init() function.
 143:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****      [..]
ARM GAS  C:\Users\ACER\AppData\Local\Temp\ccMsoCuI.s 			page 4


 144:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c **** 
 145:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****      When the compilation flag USE_HAL_COMP_REGISTER_CALLBACKS is set to 0 or
 146:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****      not defined, the callback registration feature is not available and all callbacks
 147:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c ****      are set to the corresponding weak functions.
 148:Drivers/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_comp.c **** 
